es for the later period. Based on maps found in Agrawal (1989), Kulke and Rothermund (2004) and Stein (2010).<br>"The Gupta Empire at its height controlled north and central India directly and exercised indirect control over south India. So the Gupta Empire was a smaller entity compared to the Maurya Empire."'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1554, 'temperature': 0.2})
