 the east, and within the Mekong Valley.\' \'This region incorporates the Mekong valley between Phnom Penh and the Dang Raek mountains, with lateral branches to include the drainage basin of the Tonle Sap and the Mun River valley\' \'According to Coedes, this powerful kingdom, which eventually covered a territory almost equal in extent to that of the later Khmer Empire, subsequently divided itself into a \'Land Zhenla\' that included most of Cambodia and the Khorat Plateau, and a \'Water Zhenla\', centered on the Delta.\''}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1909, 'temperature': 0.2})
